{
  "title": "Guitar Tuner FX",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "A chromatic tuner you",
        "put in a Signal Chain.",
        "It listens to the",
        "audio reaching it and",
        "shows the nearest",
        "note and how many",
        "cents off you are.",
        "",
        "Audio passes through",
        "untouched, so it can",
        "stay in your chain",
        "while you play.",
        "",
        "Typical chain:",
        " Line In > Tuner FX"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Muting",
      "lines": [
        "Knob 1, Mute Output,",
        "silences the audio",
        "coming out of the",
        "tuner, so you can",
        "tune without the",
        "room hearing you.",
        "",
        "The tuner keeps",
        "listening while muted.",
        "The Tuner page shows",
        "MUTED until you turn",
        "it back off.",
        "",
        "Switching fades over",
        "10 ms, so it never",
        "clicks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tuner Page",
      "lines": [
        "The page you land on.",
        "",
        "Big letter: the note,",
        "with its accidental",
        "and octave beside it.",
        "Right: cents and Hz.",
        "",
        "Bottom: the needle.",
        "Left is flat, right",
        "is sharp. Ticks mark",
        "10 and 25 cents. In",
        "tune (within 3 cents)",
        "the centre fills in.",
        "",
        "Right edge: the input",
        "level. If it moves but",
        "no note shows, the",
        "signal is too quiet",
        "or not a clear pitch.",
        "",
        "A note stays up for",
        "1.5 s after it fades."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Knobs",
      "lines": [
        "K1 Mute: silence the",
        " output (Off/On)",
        "K2 Acc: show notes as",
        " sharps (C#) or",
        " flats (Db)",
        "K3 Note: the reading,",
        " also as a small",
        " meter on the Main",
        " page"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Where To Put It",
      "lines": [
        "After Line In, to",
        "tune a guitar on the",
        "3.5mm input or the",
        "Move's mic.",
        "",
        "On a Move track's",
        "slot, to tune what",
        "that track plays.",
        "Needs Global Settings",
        "> Audio > Move->",
        "Schwung turned on.",
        "",
        "Range: about 70 Hz",
        "to 1200 Hz, low E on",
        "a guitar to well",
        "above the top string."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
